{"question_id": "th-004", "category": "thesis", "question": "What investable thesis do Meridian Tech Daily and Lumina funding news articulate about agent infrastructure?", "expected_answer_keywords": ["inference cost", "sub-$1", "agent"], "forbidden_keywords": [], "expected_doc_keys": ["lumina-small-model-thesis-news", "lumina-inference-funding"], "expected_abstain": false, "notes": "News synthesis plus funding strategic rationale.", "answer": "Based on the provided context, Meridian Tech Daily and Lumina's funding announcements articulate an investable thesis that a collapse in inference costs will enable widespread agentic adoption. They project that by 2027, the margin pools generated from edge inference for sub-12B models will surpass cloud training margins [C8]. This strategic outlook is reinforced by analyses demonstrating how drastically reduced small-model inference expenses are fundamentally reshaping the economics of deploying autonomous agents [C2], which directly guided Lumina's $180 million Series C raise dedicated to scaling edge inference capabilities [C1][C6].", "abstained": false, "cited_doc_keys": ["lumina-inference-funding", "lumina-small-model-thesis-news"], "retrieved_doc_keys": ["lumina-api-pricing-feb-2026", "lumina-inference-funding", "lumina-small-model-thesis-news", "lumina-spark-1-5-release", "lumina-spark-2-0-release"], "latency_s": 32.782869786024094, "tokens_used": 3237, "answer_correctness": 0.6666666666666666, "forbidden_violation": false, "evidence_recall_at_k": 1.0, "citation_precision": 1.0, "citation_faithfulness": true, "temporal_correctness": null, "supersession_correctness": null, "abstention_accuracy": true}
